          "distinct": true,
          "id": "23508c4218f59a1236ee05e68c55a40ba1780150",
          "message": "ci: Refactor benchmarks to use backrest-generated snapshot (#5347)\n\n# Ticket(s) Closed\n\n- Closes #\n\n## What\n\nRather than downloading/loading CSVs into Postgres on every run, store a\nbackrest-generated snapshot in S3 and restore them into `$PGDATA` on\nevery run.\n\nNote we only backup/restore the heap data, not the indexes (those still\nget rebuilt).\n\n## Why\n\nTo reduce CI time, which will be critical when we start adding larger\ndatasets.\n\n## How\n\n## Tests",
