          "id": "f941024979ba4abf17799fb3909ad18f5a4dd600",
          "message": "ci: Add filtered vector benchmarks (#5456)\n\n## What\n\nAdds filtered kNN variants to the Cohere vector benchmark and tunes each\nto a **~95% recall@10** operating point, so latency is measured at a\ncomparable-quality setting across dataset sizes. CI now verifies recall\nfor every query.\n\n### Queries (`benchmarks/datasets/cohere/queries/`)\nAlongside the existing unfiltered kNN, three FTS-filtered kNN queries\nselecting the top-10 nearest neighbors among rows matching a full-text\nkeyword.\n\nEach filtered query has two variants: post-filter (ANN index first) and\npre-filter (GIN index first, then sort vectors).\n\n### Probe tuning (`config.toml`)\n`ivfflat.probes` is tuned **per query and per dataset size** via binary\nsearch (forced-ANN over 100 held-out vectors vs exact ground truth),\nstored as size-keyed `[params]` and templated into the query files.\n\n`hnsw.ef_search` values are placeholders (hnsw not yet tuned — noted in\nconfig and the CI comment).\n\n### Recall in CI\n- `recall` runs a query file's **first variant** verbatim per held-out\nvector at the benchmark's operating point (qvec as a per-call constant,\nso the plan matches the latency query). Ground truth keyed as\n`ground_truth_{query}_{size}`.\n- The workflow now measures recall for **every** query discovered from\nthe `queries/` directory (previously only unfiltered) at both sizes, and\nposts a query × size table on the PR/commit.\n\n## Notes\n- Ground-truth parquets are precomputed offline (DuckDB) and uploaded to\nS3.",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-02T16:00:16-07:00",
