          "distinct": true,
          "id": "6309612631f54a79ce166f169ae0d427d13646a7",
          "message": "feat(tokenizers): expose Lindera NFKC normalization and reading-form options (#5432)\n\n# Ticket(s) Closed\n- Closes #4808\n\n## What\nAdds two Lindera tokenizer options — `nfkc` (NFKC Unicode normalization)\nand `reading_form` (Japanese / Korean reading-form) — exposed through\nthe pgrx typmod layer as fields on the existing `Lindera` tokenizer\nvariant.\n\n## Why\n#4808 asks to expose Lindera's NFKC normalization and IPADIC / ko-dic\nreading-form alignment, which the underlying `lindera` crate already\nsupports but `pg_search` did not surface. NFKC folds compatibility\ncharacters (e.g. full-width Latin letters and digits) to their canonical\nforms before segmentation; reading-form maps tokens to their kana /\nhangul reading after segmentation.\n\nThis re-submits the feature from #5140, which was closed for red CI (not\na design rejection) with an invitation to re-open once tests pass. #5140\nadded a new `SearchTokenizer::LinderaWithOptions` variant, which\nsurfaced a `lindera_with_options` row in `paradedb.tokenizers()` and\nbroke the `list_tokenizers` golden-list test. This implementation\ninstead adds the options as fields on the existing `Lindera` variant,\nmirroring the merged `keep_whitespace` template (#4481), so the\ntokenizer registry stays at 23 entries and `list_tokenizers` passes.\nCredit to @dask-58 for the original groundwork in #5140.\n\n## How\n- `nfkc` is wired as a Lindera `unicode_normalize` character filter\n(NFKC kind); `reading_form` as the `japanese_reading_form` /\n`korean_reading_form` token filters, selected by the active dictionary\n(Chinese reading-form is unsupported and returns a clear error).\n- The per-language tokenizer cache key widens from one bool\n(`keep_whitespace`) to three; `LinderaOptions::index()` packs the three\nbools into a dense `0..8` index over a per-language `OnceCell` array,\nsince each option alters the produced token stream and must be baked\ninto the cached instance.\n\n## Tests\n- `cargo test -p tokenizers lindera` — 14/14, including discriminating\noff→on cases: `ＡＢＣ１２３` → `{ABC, 123}` with NFKC; `日本語` → `{ニホンゴ}` with\nJapanese reading-form.\n- `cargo pgrx regress pg18` — `tokenizer-typmod` and\n`test_tokenizer_params` pass; `list_tokenizers` (the test #5140 broke)\npasses.\n- `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo clippy -D warnings` clean.",
